==Latin==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|ine-pro|la}} {{m|ine-pro|*ḱn̥s-eh₁-}}, {{m|ine-pro|*ḱn̥s-eie-||to announce}}. Cognate with Sanskrit {{term|शंसति|tr=śaṃsati||to declare|lang=sa}}, Proto-Iranian {{m|ira-pro|*sanh-}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|Classical}} {{IPA|/ˈkeːn.se.oː/|lang=la}}

===Verb===
{{la-verb|cēnseō|cēnsēre|cēnsuī|cēnsum|conj=2}}

# I give an [[opinion]].
# I [[think]], [[suppose]] or [[judge]].
# I [[recommend]].
#: ''Ceterum '''censeo''' Carthaginem esse delendam''
# I [[decree]], [[vote]] or [[determine]].
# I [[count]] or [[reckon]].
# I [[assess]].

